Feature: slice-3 / register-therapist-email
Branch: feat/web-app-slice-3
Verified: 2026-05-28
Anchored to: docs/18 §8.1 + §13.2 (therapist registration)

What was built
==============
- New deps: react-hook-form@7.76, @hookform/resolvers@5.4, zod@4.4.
- Form primitives: src/components/forms/Field.tsx — FieldShell,
  TextInput, Select, TextArea, Checkbox, RadioGroup. All Euphire-
  themed, reused by every Slice 3 form going forward.
- Modality catalog: src/lib/clinical/modalities.ts — typed list
  mirroring migration 000006_seed_modalities (UNIV / CBT / PSYCHO,
  all `is_supported=TRUE`). Localised labels. Swap point flagged
  for the future ListModalities RPC.
- Validation schema: src/lib/register/schema.ts — zod schema for
  the therapist email form (email, 8+digit password, names,
  modality enum, ui lang, optional title/credentials/phone,
  required ToS, optional marketing consent).
- Form component: src/components/register/TherapistEmailForm.tsx
  — full §13.2 surface in two sections (Konto + Profil). Submit
  flow:
    1. zod validate.
    2. auth.signUpWithEmail() → Firebase
       createUserWithEmailAndPassword + sendEmailVerification
       (feature 4 wiring).
    3. identityClient.createUser({firebaseUid, email,
       role=THERAPIST, firstName, lastName, uiLanguage, timezone
       from Intl, hasAcceptedTos=true}).
    4. If any optional profile fields filled →
       identityClient.updateProfile (modality + title + creds +
       phone + marketing consent). Skips the round-trip otherwise.
    5. window.location → /register/therapist/verify-email?email=…
- Verify-email page: src/app/[locale]/register/therapist/
  verify-email/page.tsx — reads ?email from search-params, shows
  "Sprawdź swoją skrzynkę" / "Check your inbox" with the address.
  ResendVerificationButton client island re-fires
  sendEmailVerification on the current Firebase user. Full
  poll-for-verified + auto-redirect logic lands in feature 5
  (email-verification-gate).
- Routes added:
    /pl/register/therapist                  (SSG)
    /en/register/therapist                  (SSG)
    /[locale]/register/therapist/verify-email (dynamic — needs
       query param)

How verified
============
1. `pnpm build` exit 0. Route table extended:
     /[locale]/register/therapist             ● SSG (×2 locales)
     /[locale]/register/therapist/verify-email ƒ Dynamic

2. HTTP smoke (Accept-Language matched):
     /register/therapist                                                   → 200
     /en/register/therapist                                                → 200
     /register/therapist/verify-email?email=anna@example.com               → 200

3. Bug caught and fixed during smoke (round-1 500 on verify-email):
   - First attempt used `t.rich("intro", { email: () => <strong> })`
     against a message containing `{email}` placeholder.
     next-intl distinguishes simple value substitution
     (`{name}` + `t(...)`) from rich rendering
     (`<name>chunks</name>` + `t.rich(...)`). Mixing caused a
     server-side render exception → 500 page.
   - Same shape error in TherapistEmailForm's consentToS Checkbox
     label.
   - Fix: simple values use `t("intro", { email: value })`
     directly; consentToS message was rewritten with `<termsLink>
     ...</termsLink>` rich placeholders so the t.rich call works.

4. Puppeteer screenshots (8 files total — 6 viewport + 2 fullPage
   + 1 verify-email fullPage):
   - register-pl-full.png: complete form, Polish copy. Top: nav +
     "REJESTRACJA · Zarejestruj się jako terapeuta · 3 darmowe
     sesje". TWOJE KONTO section: email + hasło (with hint
     "Min. 8 znaków, jedna cyfra."). TWÓJ PROFIL section: imię,
     nazwisko, główny nurt terapeutyczny (select), JĘZYK
     INTERFEJSU radio group (Polski highlighted Ember by default),
     tytuł zawodowy (with placeholder "np. Psycholog…"), numer
     prawa wykonywania zawodu, numer telefonu (placeholder
     "+48 …"). Bottom: ToS consent checkbox with Ember-underlined
     "regulamin" + "politykę prywatności" links to /legal/...,
     marketing-consent checkbox, ZAŁÓŻ KONTO submit button,
     "Masz już konto? Zaloguj się" link to app.superwizor.ai.
   - register-en-full.png: same composition, English copy.
   - register-{pl,en}-{mobile,tablet,desktop}.png: viewport-clipped
     responsiveness shots. Mobile: fields stack 1-column; tablet:
     names split into 2-col; desktop: same.
   - verify-email-pl-full.png: "Sprawdź swoją skrzynkę",
     "Wysłaliśmy link aktywacyjny na adres anna@example.com…",
     "Nie widzisz wiadomości? Sprawdź folder spam…", "WYŚLIJ
     PONOWNIE" + "Powrót do strony głównej" buttons.

5. preview_console_logs(level=error) returns "No console logs"
   after the t.rich fix.

Compliance with docs/18
=======================
- ✓ §13.2: all required fields present (email, password,
  first/last name, modality, ui language, ToS). Optional fields:
  professional_title, credentials_number, phone_number,
  marketing_consent. Not-collected-at-signup (biography, avatar,
  billing address) correctly absent.
- ✓ §8.1 email/password path: createUserWithEmailAndPassword →
  sendEmailVerification → "We sent you a confirmation email" page
  matches the design.
- ✓ §13.1 form conventions: zod-validated client-side, inline
  errors per field, submit disabled while in flight.
- ✓ §14.5: zero hard-coded UI strings. Form labels, hints,
  errors, section titles, button text all route through
  useTranslations.
- ✓ Login link cross-origin to app.superwizor.ai per §5 R3.

Known gaps (deferred)
=====================
- No Google OAuth path on this page yet — feature 2.
- Verify-email page is a static "check your inbox" interstitial.
  Polling for emailVerified + auto-redirect to
  app.superwizor.ai/login lands in feature 5.
- Backend live submission untested in-session — no identity-svc
  running. The Connect-RPC call paths are typed against the real
  proto (CreateUserRequestSchema + UpdateProfileRequestSchema
  from gen/ts) so type drift would surface at build, not at
  runtime. Feature 8 (registration-e2e-playwright) covers the
  end-to-end happy path against a live emulator + httptest stub.
- ListModalities RPC doesn't exist; static catalog mirrors
  migration. Same swap-point pattern as plans.ts.

